  "body": "Stacked on [REC PR #93](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/rec_bianchi/pull/93), parent `2c4627bf480a306f34bb35d0ec5a3d18182b170e`. This is **actual original HyRec2012 H+He FULL FLRW native-C recombination at a REI-matched cosmological background**, producing an **optional, disabled zbar=20 REI initial-condition sensitivity candidate**. It is NOT an independent Python R3c FULL history or a new REI native run.\n\n**Actual result and source identity**\n- Original unmodified HyRec2012 ZIP SHA256 `48cd597519606cdafd0ee6405b781d28467cd323278d16596055a8d0577a1d27`, recompiled GCC `-O3 -fno-fast-math`, source-executed 8001 redshift rows, 3 input-YHe runs, original output SHA `6fa5cb83a45ed3599d824ff821b6c8df41dd6d0e78a46cf9b33fde91b933e400`.\n- Source REI `SCENARIO_LOCK.json` SHA `07aa11d2d3fd47d2ed95e9d9161f6205e4d9ba386c27ad43d2b298fcd86d1696`. Match (h=.674,\\Omega_m=.315,\\Omega_r=.000092,Y_He=.2454,\\omega_bh^2=.0224,T_0=2.7255 K), effective massless source radiation `N_eff=3.03821934419124` to reproduce *total* REI H(z). Original HyRec vs REI nH0 and fHe convention differences explicitly retained (-0.054115% donor nH).\n- zbar20 actual native FULL source `x_e=0.000210349192936,T_m=9.306042400380866 K`; original REI conditional baseline `x_HII=0.000200000,Tgas=8.098143045064857 K`. Candidate differences +5.1746% electrons, +14.9158% T. At fixed recipient nH: local `d tau / d ln a` +5.1746%, energy density +14.9169%. These are **instant initial coefficients**, not integrated optical depth or reheated REI observables.\n- Real YHe\u00b1.002 separate original-C source reruns, 1 vs 2 worker byte-identical per case; observed 1.444\u00d7 2-worker speedup vs serial sum. Vectorized 1581-row initial electron/opacity/thermal postprocessing 29.88\u00d7 scalar with 3.92e-16 relative residual. **Neither is a native REI solver speedup**.\n- Theoretical limit: REI qref signed prescribed density-fixed Bianchi I is scoped zbar20\u21924. Formal back-extrapolation qref=-.01 to z600 gives s/H=-.81695 and H_parallel/H=-.63391; at z1100 H_parallel/H=-.91467. Wolfram verifies condition s<-Hflrw/sqrt(3). This is an *outside-domain diagnostic*, NOT a general Bianchi recombination no-go or valid signed-q high-z history.\n- `REI_DONOR_CANDIDATE_OPTIN_ONLY.json` is explicitly `DISABLED_REQUIRES_SEPARATE_REI_SENSITIVITY_CAMPAIGN` and preserves original REI ionizing photon stock zero. Source helium x_e\u2192HII projection assumes late He-neutral C source branch, not independently resolved helium species.\n- Local targeted **7 PASS** including fresh rebuilt original C; full REC **474 PASS/41 SKIP**, quick repo gate PASS within inherited dynamic macro-ownership HOLD. Original dirty REC and native running REI producer/checkpoints unmodified. No local Codex.\n- Original binary/source, native output gzip, true history CSV, plots, SHA/provenance, parameter sensitivities, report, tests and next actions at `research/rec_r3c_rei_bridge_20261015/`.\n\n**Not admitted:** altered REI abundance/temperature evolution or tau, primordial signed Bianchi recombination, native REI source adoption, and the still-open independent REC Python FULL accepted-history H-only trajectory. Next action: separate REI isolated sensitivity run *from fresh zbar20 initial state* with native chemistry/RT ledgers and paired q0/signed comparisons; preserve baseline. Draft stacked PR, no merge.",
